    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="d43-01" n="1" xml:id="d43-01"/>

                <head>43. Memorandum of Telephone Conversation Between the Under Secretary of State
                    for Public Affairs (Richardson) and the
                    Presidentʼs Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d43-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d43-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1969-02-20">February 20, 1969,
                        noon</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>K said President wants to have Relief Coordinator for Biafra but wants him
                    appointed outside of State Department—not a State Department official. R said he
                    would like to discuss this at lunch as well as Peru.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Library of Congress, Manuscript Division, Kissinger Papers, Box 359, Telephone Conversations,
                    Chronological File. No classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d43-f2" n="2" xml:id="d43-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Kissinger told Richardson that the President wanted the Relief
                    Coordinator to come from outside the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
